verned deployment of capability that cannot be rolled back — and no one funded, scoped, or standing to stop it.\n\nOne narrower point, because the Skeptic anticipated it correctly. Swap compute for a single behavior benchmark and you have relocated the gaming problem to a number developers optimize around. I grant that too — a single scalar gate is a design failure. The answer is not one score but a portfolio of indicators plus adversarial red-teaming keyed to capability combinations, because catastrophic risk emerges from what capabilities do together, not from any one metric read alone. A gameable single benchmark refutes bad gate design. It does not refute gating.",
